$CATEGORY: Vocabulary/HansenQuinn/4

::Q001::[markdown]δίκη, δίκης, ἡ:{
	~%-100%beginning#Incorrect. **ἀρχή, ἀρχῆς, ἡ** means “beginning” (Chapter 4).
	~%-100%chorus#Incorrect. **χορός, χοροῦ, ὁ** means “chorus” (Chapter 6).
	~%100%justice#Correct: **δίκη, δίκης, ἡ** → “justice” (Chapter 4).
	~%-100%thing#Incorrect. **χρῆμα, χρημάτος, τό** means “thing” (Chapter 8).
	~%-100%beauty#Incorrect. **κάλλος, κάλλους, τό** means “beauty” (Chapter 11).
	~%-100%teacher#Incorrect. **διδάσκαλος, διδασκάλου, ὁ** means “teacher” (Chapter 5).
	~%-100%rule#Incorrect. **ἀρχή, ἀρχῆς, ἡ** means “rule” (Chapter 4).
	~%-100%road#Incorrect. **ὁδός, ὁδοῦ, ἡ** means “road” (Chapter 1).
}


::Q002::[markdown]just:{
	~%-100%εὐτυκής, εὐτυκές#Incorrect. **εὐτυκής, εὐτυκές** means “lucky” (Chapter 11).
	~%-100%καλός, καλή, καλόν#Incorrect. **καλός, καλή, καλόν** means “beautiful” (Chapter 4).
	~%-100%αἴτιος αἰτία αἴτιον#Incorrect. **αἴτιος αἰτία αἴτιον** means “responsible (for) + gen.” (Chapter 11).
	~%-100%εὐγενής, εὑγενές#Incorrect. **εὐγενής, εὑγενές** means “well-born” (Chapter 10).
	~%100%δίκαιος, δικαίᾱ, δίκαιον#Correct: **δίκαιος, δικαίᾱ, δίκαιον** → “just” (Chapter 4).
	~%-100%εὐδαίμων, εὔδαιμον#Incorrect. **εὐδαίμων, εὔδαιμον** means “fortunate” (Chapter 10).
	~%-100%αἰσχρός, αἰσχρά, αἰσχρόν#Incorrect. **αἰσχρός, αἰσχρά, αἰσχρόν** means “ugly” (Chapter 7).
	~%-100%ἄλογος, ἄλογον#Incorrect. **ἄλογος, ἄλογον** means “unreasonable” (Chapter 9).
}


::Q003::[markdown]Which Principal Part of ἐθέλω is ‘ἠθέλησα’?:{
	~%-100%5th#Incorrect. **ἠθέλησα** is the 3rd Principal Part of **ἐθέλω**, not the 5th.
	~%-100%4th#Incorrect. **ἠθέλησα** is the 3rd Principal Part of **ἐθέλω**, not the 4th.
	~%-100%6th#Incorrect. **ἠθέλησα** is the 3rd Principal Part of **ἐθέλω**, not the 6th.
	~%100%3rd#Correct: **ἠθέλησα** is the 3rd Principal Part of **ἐθέλω** (Chapter 4).
	~%-100%2nd#Incorrect. **ἠθέλησα** is the 3rd Principal Part of **ἐθέλω**, not the 2nd.
	~%-100%1st#Incorrect. **ἠθέλησα** is the 3rd Principal Part of **ἐθέλω**, not the 1st.
}


::Q004::[markdown]Pick the 1st Principal Part of τάττω.:{
	~%100%τάττω#Correct: **τάττω** is the 1st Principal Part of **τάττω** (Chapter 4).
	~%-100%θάπτω#Incorrect. **θάπτω** is Principal Part 1 of **θάπτω** “bury” (Chapter 4).
	~%-100%τάξω#Incorrect. **τάξω** is Principal Part 2 of **τάττω** “draw up (in battle)” (Chapter 4).
	~%-100%τέταγμαι#Incorrect. **τέταγμαι** is Principal Part 5 of **τάττω** “draw up (in battle)” (Chapter 4).
	~%-100%ἔταξα#Incorrect. **ἔταξα** is Principal Part 3 of **τάττω** “draw up (in battle)” (Chapter 4).
	~%-100%ἐτάχθην#Incorrect. **ἐτάχθην** is Principal Part 6 of **τάττω** “draw up (in battle)” (Chapter 4).
	~%-100%φυλάττω#Incorrect. **φυλάττω** is Principal Part 1 of **φυλάττω** “guard” (Chapter 3).
	~%-100%τέταχα#Incorrect. **τέταχα** is Principal Part 4 of **τάττω** “draw up (in battle)” (Chapter 4).
}


::Q005::[markdown]ἔθαψα:{
	~%-100%be spoken of#Incorrect. **ἀκούω** is Principal Part 1 of **ἀκούω** “be spoken of” (Chapter 11).
	~%-100%think worthy of#Incorrect. **ἀξιόω** is Principal Part 1 of **ἀξιόω** “think worthy of” (Chapter 10).
	~%100%bury#Correct: **ἔθαψα** is Principal Part 3 of **θάπτω** “bury” (Chapter 4).
	~%-100%prevent#Incorrect. **κωλύω** is Principal Part 1 of **κωλύω** “prevent” (Chapter 6).
	~%-100%draw up (in battle)#Incorrect. **τάττω** is Principal Part 1 of **τάττω** “draw up (in battle)” (Chapter 4).
	~%-100%stay#Incorrect. **μένω** is Principal Part 1 of **μένω** “stay” (Chapter 10).
	~%-100%do#Incorrect. **πράττω** is Principal Part 1 of **πράττω** “do” (Chapter 5).
}


::Q006::[markdown]after:{
	~%-100%ὑπέρ + acc#Incorrect. **ὑπέρ + acc** means “(of motion or measure) over” (Chapter 9).
	~%-100%σύv + dative#Incorrect. **σύv + dative** means “with” (Chapter 4).
	~%-100%παρά + acc#Incorrect. **παρά + acc** means “to the side of” (Chapter 2).
	~%-100%παρά + dat#Incorrect. **παρά + dat** means “at the side of” (Chapter 2).
	~%100%ἐπεί#Correct: **ἐπεί** → “after” (Chapter 3).
	~%-100%μετά + gen.#Incorrect. **μετά + gen.** means “with” (Chapter 4).
	~%-100%ἄνευ#Incorrect. **ἄνευ** means “without” (Chapter 7).
}


